    "details": "Designed by VelvetDigitalLabb with the help of AI tools, based on my own creative direction and brief.\n\nKNOW WHAT YOUR BRAND STANDS FOR, BEFORE YOU DESIGN OR WRITE A WORD\n\nThe Brand Strategy Workbook is a 31-page Canva workbook that takes you from \"I know what I do, but I can't explain why it's different\" to a clear, written brand strategy you can hand to any designer, copywriter or team member.\n\nBY THE END YOU'LL HAVE\n✓ A positioning statement you can say out loud\n✓ A brand personality your whole team agrees on\n✓ A clear picture of your ideal client and the objections to answer\n✓ A tagline and elevator pitch in your own words\n✓ A one-page Brand Strategy on a Page you can share\n✓ A 90-day plan to put it all to work\n\nSTART WITH THE BRAND CLARITY SCORE\nPage 4 is a quick self-check: six statements, rated 1 to 5. Your score tells you where to spend your time, so you never start from a blank page.\n\nWHAT'S INSIDE: 5 GUIDED PARTS\n• Part 1 · Foundation: mission, vision and values, origin story, the problem you solve, who you help (and who you don't)\n• Part 2 · Audience: target audience profile, pain points and desires, objections and trust blockers\n• Part 3 · Position: competitive landscape, positioning statement, positioning map, three brand pillars\n• Part 4 · Personality: personality sliders, 12 brand archetypes to choose from, messaging pillars, tagline and elevator pitch\n• Part 5 · Activate: brand story framework, proof bank, brand touchpoints, 90-day activation plan, Brand Strategy on a Page\n\nEach part opens with what you'll have by the end and a suggested pace, so you always know where you are.\n\n3 COLOR VERSIONS INCLUDED\nClassic (ivory, forest green and gold), Light (warm white, plum and blush) and Dark (midnight and champagne gold). Same 31 pages, three looks. Use one or all three.\n\nALSO INCLUDED: CUSTOMER GUIDE (PDF, 12 PAGES) + PRINTABLE PDFs\nThe guide holds your Canva template links and covers setup, editing tips, two filled-in worked examples (a Brand Clarity Score and a positioning statement, both completed), a client workflow for designers, copywriters and consultants, printing tips, troubleshooting and a license summary. You also get a printable PDF of each color version.\n\nWHO IT'S FOR\nFreelancers, coaches, small studios and small business owners who want clarity before they build a website or a logo. Designers, copywriters and consultants can also use it as a structured brand discovery tool with clients.\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n1. Purchase and download your files from Etsy (use a web browser; the Etsy app doesn't offer downloads)\n2. Open the guide and click the version you want\n3. Click \"Use template\" to make your own editable copy in Canva\n4. Type your answers, or print and write by hand\n\nTHIS IS THE THINKING, NOT THE DESIGN\nThe workbook defines your strategy: who you serve, how you're different and how you sound. It does not create a logo or a visual identity. Once your strategy is set, plan your site with the Website Blueprint Kit and write it with the Website Content Planner (both in the VelvetDigitalLabb shop).\n\nGOOD TO KNOW\n- Instant digital download. Nothing is shipped.\n- A4 format. On a US Letter printer, choose \"Fit to page\".\n- Editable in Canva. Fonts used: Playfair Display and Inter.\n- Personal and client projects are allowed. Reselling or sharing the template file or its link is not.",
