    "details": "A PORTFOLIO WEBSITE THAT LOOKS PREMIUM, WITH NO BUILDER AND NO MONTHLY FEE\n\nAtelier is a complete, hand-coded website template for freelance designers, developers, consultants and small studios. Change the words and pictures, upload the folder to a free host, and your site is live. No WordPress, no website builder, no subscription.\n\nWHAT YOU GET\n• 9 pages: Home, Work (with category filter), Project page, Services & pricing, About, Contact, plus a Thank-you page, a 404 page and a Privacy notice\n• 3 colour versions in one download: Ivory, Sage and Midnight (dark)\n• Customer guide (PDF, 14 pages) for Mac and Windows: open, edit, connect the form, publish for free, add your domain, launch checklist, troubleshooting\n• Licence and font licences\n• Instant download\n\nFEATURES\n• Responsive: designed for phone, tablet and desktop, with a clean mobile menu\n• Contact form ready to connect to a free form service such as Formspree\n• Private by design: fonts are included, so nothing is loaded from Google or other outside servers. No cookies, no trackers\n• Search-friendly basics already set up: page titles, descriptions, sitemap, robots.txt, social preview image and structured data\n• Accessible: skip link, keyboard navigation, readable colour contrast, reduced-motion support\n• Easy to edit: friendly \"EDIT:\" notes in the files tell you what to change, line by line\n• Plain HTML, CSS and a little JavaScript: no frameworks, no build tools, nothing to install\n\nWHAT YOU NEED (NOT INCLUDED)\n• A free plain-text editor (the guide recommends one)\n• A place to publish. The guide shows two free options step by step\n• Optional: your own domain name (usually a small yearly fee)\n• A form service to receive messages. Free plans exist; check their current limits\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n1. Purchase and download your files from Etsy (use a web browser; the Etsy app doesn't offer downloads)\n2. Unzip the folder and double-click index.html to see your website\n3. Pick your favourite colour version and delete the other two\n4. Replace the example text, photos and project pictures with your own\n5. Connect the contact form, then publish. The guide covers every step\n\nWHO IT'S FOR\nFreelance web designers and developers, graphic designers, photographers, writers, coaches, consultants and small studios who want a polished website of their own.\n\nGOOD TO KNOW\n- Instant digital download. Nothing is shipped.\n- The template is in English. The names, companies, quotes and prices in it are fictional placeholders for you to replace.\n- This is a template of files, not a hosted website. Domain, hosting and a form service are separate.\n- Licence: use it for one website per purchase, either your own or one client's. You can change anything. Reselling, sharing or uploading the template files is not allowed. Need several client sites? Buy one copy per site.\n- The privacy page is a general starting point, not legal advice.\n- The included illustrations are abstract designs for the template. Replace them with your own work when you can.",
