    "details": "Designed by VelvetDigitalLabb with the help of AI tools, based on my own creative direction and brief.\n\nA DEVELOPER PORTFOLIO THAT PEOPLE REMEMBER\n\nDevFolio is a complete, hand-coded portfolio website template for developers, DevOps and cloud engineers, cybersecurity and IT professionals, students and freelancers. It does what a normal template can't: visitors can type commands in a real working terminal on your site, jump anywhere with a command palette, and switch the whole look with one click.\n\nWOW FEATURES\n- Interactive terminal: visitors type help, about, skills, projects, contact, even sudo hire me\n- Command palette: press Ctrl+K (Cmd+K on Mac) to search and jump anywhere\n- 4 themes in one download: Terminal green, Cyber purple, Midnight blue and Light. Visitors can switch with one click\n- Animated falling-code background, typed job titles, animated skill bars and counters\n- Project cards with 3D tilt and category filters\n- Career timeline and contact form\n\nSUPER EASY TO EDIT\nEverything personal lives in ONE file (config.js): your name, bio, links, skills, projects and experience. Change the text, save, refresh. No coding knowledge needed.\n\nWHAT YOU GET\n- The complete website (HTML, CSS, JavaScript)\n- Customer guide (PDF, 9 pages) for Mac and Windows: open it, edit it, add your CV, publish for free, connect the contact form, troubleshooting, launch checklist\n- Licence and font licences\n- Instant download\n\nBUILT THE RIGHT WAY\n- Responsive and mobile first: phone, tablet and desktop\n- Fast and private: fonts included, nothing loaded from Google or other outside servers, no cookies, no trackers\n- Plain HTML, CSS and a little JavaScript: no frameworks, no build tools, nothing to install\n- Accessible touches: keyboard-friendly, visible focus, reduced-motion support for visitors who prefer less animation\n- Works on any hosting: the guide shows free hosting step by step\n\nWHAT YOU NEED (NOT INCLUDED)\n- A free plain-text editor (already on your computer)\n- A place to publish. The guide shows a free option (Netlify Drop) step by step\n- Optional: your own domain name (usually a small yearly fee)\n- A form service to receive messages (the guide uses Formspree; free plans exist, check their current limits)\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n1. Purchase and download your files from Etsy (use a web browser; the Etsy app doesn't offer downloads)\n2. Unzip and double-click index.html to see your portfolio\n3. Open assets/js/config.js and replace the example details with yours\n4. Publish for free and share your link on your CV and LinkedIn\n\nGOOD TO KNOW\n- Instant digital download. Nothing is shipped.\n- The template is in English. The name, companies, projects and numbers in it are fictional placeholders for you to replace.\n- This is a template of files, not a hosted website. Domain, hosting and a form service are separate.\n- Licence: use it for your own portfolio or for one client site per purchase. You can change anything. Reselling, sharing or uploading the template files is not allowed.\n- Designed for current versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox.\n- Mentions of other companies' services (Netlify, Formspree) are for guidance only; no affiliation.",
