    "details": "Designed by VelvetDigitalLabb with the help of AI tools, based on my own creative direction and brief.\n\nA LANDING PAGE THAT MAKES YOUR PRODUCT LOOK FUNDED\n\nLaunchpad is a complete, hand-coded landing page template for SaaS products, apps, AI tools and startups. Present your product, show your pricing and collect waitlist signups by email. It looks like a page a design agency would charge thousands for, and you edit everything in one simple file.\n\nWOW FEATURES\n• Live animated dashboard in the hero: numbers count up, the chart moves, new activity slides in. Pure code, no video\n• Aurora light background and glowing gradient headline\n• Bento feature grid with a spotlight that follows the mouse: AI chat that types, live sync, orbiting integrations, forecasts\n• Pricing with a Monthly / Yearly switch and animated prices, plus an animated border on the most popular plan\n• Scrolling logo strip and two rows of moving testimonial cards\n• Dark and light mode (visitors can switch) and 3 colour presets: Violet, Emerald, Sunset\n\nEVERY SECTION YOU NEED\nHero with waitlist form, dashboard preview, logo strip, features, how it works, stats, pricing, testimonials, FAQ, final call to action, footer, plus a ready privacy page.\n\nSUPER EASY TO EDIT\nAll your content lives in ONE file (config.js): brand, headline, features, prices, questions, footer links, even the privacy text. Change the words, save, refresh. No coding knowledge needed.\n\nWHAT YOU GET\n• The complete landing page (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) and a privacy page\n• Customer guide (PDF, 9 pages) for Mac and Windows: edit, change colours, publish for free, collect signups, troubleshooting, launch checklist\n• Licence and font licences\n• Instant download\n\nBUILT THE RIGHT WAY\n• Responsive and mobile first, with a mobile menu\n• Fast and private: fonts included, nothing loaded from Google or outside servers, no cookies, no trackers\n• Plain HTML, CSS and a little JavaScript: no frameworks, no build tools, nothing to install\n• Accessible touches: keyboard-friendly, visible focus, reduced-motion support\n\nWHAT YOU NEED (NOT INCLUDED)\n• A free plain-text editor (already on your computer)\n• A place to publish. The guide shows a free option (Netlify Drop) step by step\n• Optional: your own domain name (usually a small yearly fee)\n• A form service to receive signups (the guide uses Formspree; free plans exist, check their current limits)\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n1. Purchase and download your files from Etsy (use a web browser; the Etsy app doesn't offer downloads)\n2. Unzip and double-click index.html to see your landing page\n3. Open assets/js/config.js and write your own content\n4. Publish for free and start collecting signups\n\nGOOD TO KNOW\n- Instant digital download. Nothing is shipped.\n- The template is in English. The brand \"Pulsar\", company names, quotes, ratings and numbers are fictional samples: replace them with your real content before publishing.\n- This is a template of files, not a hosted website. Domain, hosting and a form service are separate.\n- Licence: use it for your own product or for one client site per purchase. You can change anything. Reselling, sharing or uploading the template files is not allowed.\n- The privacy page is a starting point, not legal advice.\n- Designed for current versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox.\n- Mentions of other companies' services (Netlify, Formspree) are for guidance only; no affiliation.",
